            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 71-year-old male patient, admitted on 12/08/2008 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Spirometry supported the diagnosis of severe obstructive ventilatory impairment. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory changes. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. He responded well to treatment with clinical improvement and stabilisation of oxygen saturation. Discharge education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided. He is discharged in a stable condition and I would kindly ask you to continue outpatient COPD management and follow-up. Yours sincerely.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
